-- `States`, propositions (`Axiom`, `Theorem`, `Conjecture`), `Example`, and
-- every structural clause group in realistic mathematical context.


-- `States` defines a named proposition with a `that:` body. The `States:`
-- section itself is a marker; documentation lives under `Appendix:`.
[\commutes:in{M ::= (X, *)}:with{y}]
States:
when:
. M is \magma
. y "in" M
that:
. forAll: x "in" M
  then: x * y = y * x
Appendix:
. called: "$y?$ commutes with every element of $M?$"
. description: "States that $y$ lies in the center of the magma $M$."
Id: "bc970e75-9dfb-4274-b470-6fa57ea77741"


-- An anonymous theorem with `given:`, `where:`, and `Proof:`.
Theorem:
given:
. A, B, C is \set
where:
. A \:subset:/ B
. B \:subset:/ C
. A \:subset?:/ C
then:
. forAll: x "in" A
  then: x "in"? C
Proof: "Any element {. x "in" A .} satisfies {. x "in"? B .} and hence
        {. x "in"? C .}."
Appendix:
. called: "transitivity of subset inclusion"
Id: "1706b3ba-b789-448c-a5c4-d2bc619e1933"


-- With a command heading, an `Axiom` registers a signature that prose can cite
-- with `{: \extensionality.axiom :}` and `have:` can cite with `by:`.
[\extensionality.axiom]
Axiom:
given: A, B is \set
then:
. have: A = B
  iff:
  . forAll: x "in" A
    then: x "in"? B
  . forAll: y "in" B
    then: y "in"? A
Appendix:
. called: "axiom of extensionality"
Id: "d570056b-6eb9-41fb-8284-4adbe6ddeda8"


-- A `Conjecture` states an unproven hypothesis about real or natural numbers.
[\collatz.like.hypothesis]
Conjecture:
given: n is \natural
then:
. exists: m is \natural
  suchThat:
  . anyOf:
    . n + m = n
    . m + \one != \zero
Appendix:
. called: "an illustrative number-theoretic conjecture"
Id: "e6d5caf7-f4bf-4333-8e6f-b3c65d38cfb2"


-- `iff:` states a biconditional theorem characterizing mutual inclusion.
Theorem:
given: A, B is \set
then: A = B
iff:
. A \:subset?:/ B
. B \:subset?:/ A
Appendix:
. called: "double inclusion characterizes set equality"
Id: "862537de-6ab3-4b30-b4e9-2651927ab166"


-- Every structural clause group (`allOf:`, `anyOf:`, `oneOf:`, `not:`,
-- `forAll:` with `where:`, `exists:`, `existsUnique:`, `if:`,
-- `let:`, `equivalently:`, `piecewise:` with `elseIf:`, and `have:`/`iff:`)
-- demonstrated on real arithmetic and group algebra.
Theorem:
given:
. G ::= (X, *, e) is \group
. x, y is \real
. A, U is \set
where: A \:subset:/ U
then:
. allOf:
  . x + y = y + x
  . anyOf:
    . x < y
    . oneOf:
      . x = y
      . not: x = y
. forAll: a "in" X
  where:
  . a != e
  . a "in"? X
  then: a * e = a
. exists: b "in" X
  suchThat: a_id := b * e = b
. existsUnique: id "in" X
  suchThat:
  . forAll: a "in" X
    then: id * a = a
. if: x < y
  then: y != x
. let: s := x + y
  where: s is \real
  then: s - y = x
. equivalently:
  . x = y
  . x - y = \natural.to.real{\zero}
. piecewise:
  if: x < \natural.to.real{\zero}
  then: \abs{x} = -x
  elseIf: x = \natural.to.real{\zero}
  then: \abs{x} = \natural.to.real{\zero}
  else: \abs{x} = x
. have: x + (-x) = \natural.to.real{\zero}
  iff: -x + x = \natural.to.real{\zero}
Appendix:
. called: "clauses in real arithmetic and group theory"
Id: "85a7e92b-f346-4d3c-b618-b64c9b683d71"


-- A `have:`/`asserting:` group discharges a step with local assumptions and
-- records `by:` theorem references and `because:` prose or clauses.
Theorem:
given:
. A, B is \set
where:
. A \:subset:/ B
. B \:subset:/ A
then:
. have: A = B
  asserting:
  . forAll: x "in" A
    then: x "in"? B
  . forAll: y "in" B
    then: y "in"? A
  by: \extensionality.axiom
  because: "Two sets with identical elements are equal by extensionality."
Appendix:
. called: "mutual subsets are equal"
Id: "9539b3b1-6b22-4a24-8fd2-84f87f9f8f5d"


-- An `Example:` interleaves checked mathematical clauses with explanatory prose.
[\identity.composition.example]
Example:
. "Take any set $X$ and form its identity function."
. forAll: X is \set
  then:
  . let: id := \identity:on{X}
    then:
    . forAll: x "in" X
      then: id(x) = x
. "Applying the unit clamping triple's identity clamp to a real value preserves it."
. forAll: r "in" \reals.set
  then: \abs{r} = \abs{r}
Appendix:
. metadata:
  . version: "1.0"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-6666-4aaa-8bbb-000000000001"
